#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_set

#% text
# `bit_set(k, i)` gives the integer k with bit i (0 the least significant) set to 1.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Negative integers count in two's complement, as for `bit_or`. Lists thread over k.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_set(42, 0)
#% output
#= 43

#% cell
bit_set(42, 9)
#% output
#= 554

#% cell
fold(bit_set, 0, [1, 3, 7])
#% output
#= 138

#% cell
bit_set([0, 1, 2, 3], 2)
#% output
#= [4, 5, 6, 7]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_clear`, `bit_flip`, `bit_or`
